  {
   "title": "Newspaper vocabulary added",
   "text": "30,791 of the reference words come from a newspaper corpus (Leipzig Corpora Collection, pus_news_2020_100K, 2.6 million words); 2,732 come from the subtitle list. Written sources are more formal than subtitles and contain more names and foreign words. Frequencies of the corpus-only words come from that corpus and are not comparable with subtitle frequencies."
  },
  {
   "title": "Abjad: CV is orthographic",
